  Both hypotheses confirmed with perfect results: the improved search algorithm (with adaptive KV ceiling detection) achieved 100% Pareto coverage across all 4 regimes and both random seeds, exceeding the ≥90% and ≥85% thresholds predicted. All 8 test conditions (4 regimes × 2 seeds) hit 100% coverage within exactly 200 evaluations each.

  * h-main CONFIRMED: Pareto coverage was 100% in all 4 regimes at seed=42 (qwen3-14b/rate=100: 26/26, Llama-70B/rate=100: 28/28, qwen3-14b/rate=200: 27/27, qwen3-14b/rate=50: 18/18), well above the ≥90% threshold, using only 200 evaluations per regime.
  * h-robustness CONFIRMED: At seed=123, coverage remained 100% across all 4 regimes (0 percentage-point difference vs seed=42), far exceeding the ≥85% threshold and ≤10pp variance bound. Pareto front sizes shifted between seeds (e.g., 26→28 for qwen3-14b/rate=100) but the algorithm found all reference configs regardless.
  * The key algorithmic fix — using kv=max(KV_VALUES)=10000 in Phase 1 instead of a hardcoded kv=5000 — makes the search model-agnostic. Llama-70B's effective ceiling at kv=3000 is correctly detected, and Phase 2 fills intermediate values that are Pareto-optimal for different model topologies.
  * No surprises or failures: the algorithm found 30–39 Pareto configs per run (vs 18–28 in the exhaustive reference), with the surplus being non-dominated but outside the reference set due to additional KV values explored. The search generalizes cleanly across model sizes (14B vs 70B) and arrival rates (50, 100, 200).

